        "id": "q-1792355944352-160",
        "text": "Team, here is the exact verified schema of the `public.orders` table from Supabase:\n- `id` (uuid)\n- `user_id` (uuid)\n- `total_amount` (numeric)\n- `status` (text)\n- `razorpay_order_id` (text)\n- `razorpay_payment_id` (text)\n- `items` (jsonb)\n- `created_at` (timestamp with time zone)\n- `youpi_order_id` (text)\n- `youpi_payment_id` (text)\n- `youpi_utr` (text)\n\nPlease fix the UPI order creation lifecycle with these exact columns:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Stop Order Creation on QR Generation\nIn `UpiPaymentModal.tsx` / `Checkout.tsx`:\n- When the UPI QR modal opens or generates the QR code, DO NOT call `supabase.from('orders').insert(...)`.\n- QR generation should strictly keep the temporary session in memory or `upi_payment_sessions`. No row in `orders` table yet!\n\n---\n\n### 2. Insert Order ONLY on UTR Submission\nWhen the customer enters their 12-digit UTR and clicks the \"Submit / Verify Payment\" button:\n1. Validate that UTR is entered and exactly 12 digits.\n2. Insert into `public.orders` using the correct column name (`youpi_utr`):\n```ts\nconst { data, error } = await supabase\n  .from('orders')\n  .insert({\n    user_id: user.id,\n    total_amount: orderAmount,\n    status: 'PENDING_VERIFICATION',\n    youpi_utr: utrValue.trim(),\n    youpi_order_id: currentSessionId || null,\n    items: cartItems\n  });",
        "ts": 1792355944352
      }
